(vector (map (:adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-dependency-6419 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies uniquely names :banking/:swift (pointing at kotoba-lang/banking, kotoba-lang/swift), but this R0 implementation deliberately does NOT add either as a real deps.edn dependency -- following every sibling actor's established posture of implementing the specific ground-truth check a governor needs directly (the real IBAN checksum, in this case) rather than pulling in an external capability library for a governed-actor scaffold this narrow in scope"), (:adr/pattern-6419 "sealed Banking Advisor + independent Monetary Intermediation Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all fifty-two prior actors; THIRTY-NINTH build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569)"), (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530/6820/6612/6492/6920/6611/7120/8620/8530/9200/7500/9603/9521/9321/8730/9102/9103/9602/9000/8890/8610/9311/8510/9412/6491/8720/8521/6619/3600/6190/3030/3830/7020/9420/9491/2610/3512/8810/8691/8569 ADR-0001s" "langgraph-clj ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607081800"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 52, :blueprint 32, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/portability-lesson-6419 "a first draft of the mod-97 computation used JVM-only Character/isDigit, Character/toUpperCase and int-on-char arithmetic, which would silently misbehave if this .cljc namespace were ever compiled for ClojureScript -- caught and rewritten before any test was run to use portable clojure.string-based digit lookups instead, the same .cljc portability discipline this repo's own CLAUDE.md instructions established for kotoba wasm/clojurewasm/cljs/nbb/jvm priority"), (:adr/test-status-6419 "38 tests / 176 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean dual-actuation lifecycle plus five HARD-hold cases), plus a repointed pre-existing kotoba-lang/industry fixture test suite (7 tests / 101 assertions, all green)"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607081800: `cloud-itonami-isic-6419` (community monetary intermediation) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607081500 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8810`, community care coordination)\n- ADR-2607081600 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8691`, health access navigation)\n- ADR-2607081700 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8569`, community learning support)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-6419/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph-clj` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-6419` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\ncommunity banking: deposit and account operations, lending, interbank\nmessaging, clearing and settlement. Like every prior vertical in this\nfleet, the blueprint text alone is not an implementation — this ADR\nrecords the governed-actor build that promotes\n`cloud-itonami-isic-6419` from `:blueprint` to `:implemented` in the\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry, the thirty-ninth vertical built\noutside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-6419`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   community-banking operating model (account intake, AML/KYC\n   assessment, sanctions screening, settlement posting, interbank-\n   message dispatch) but had no governed-actor implementation: no\n   Store, no Governor, no rollout phasing, no tests.\n2. The blueprint's own Minimum Production Controls name a concrete,\n   verifiable requirement not seen in any prior sibling: \"IBAN mod-97\n   verification before any external transfer\" — this needed a REAL\n   algorithm, not a fabricated placeholder, unlike every prior check\n   family in this fleet (which compare two already-trusted fields\n   against each other or a threshold).\n3. `blueprint.edn` carried a stale pre-rename `:itonami.blueprint/id`\n   (`\"cloud-itonami-6419\"`, missing the `isic-` infix) and was missing\n   `:robotics` from its `:required-technologies` vector despite\n   `:itonami.blueprint/robotics true` already being set separately.\n4. This blueprint's `:required-technologies` uniquely names `:banking`/\n   `:swift` as required capability libraries — a decision was needed\n   on whether to add `kotoba-lang/banking`/`kotoba-lang/swift` as real\n   code dependencies or follow the fleet's established self-contained\n   convention.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `account`. Five ops:\n   `:account/intake`, `:compliance/verify`, `:sanctions/screen`,\n   `:actuation/post-settlement` (high-stakes), and `:actuation/\n   dispatch-interbank-message` (high-stakes) — a dual-actuation-on-\n   one-entity shape grounded directly in the blueprint's own Core\n   Contract diagram and Trust Controls.\n2. **`iban-checksum-invalid?` — the FIRST checksum/format-validity\n   check, a real algorithm.** `banking.registry` implements ISO 7064\n   MOD 97-10 (rearrange, letter-substitute A=10..Z=35, mod 97, valid\n   iff remainder = 1) against the account's own IBAN field — no\n   fabricated placeholder, tested against well-known published IBAN\n   examples (Deutsche Bundesbank's own `DE89370400440532013000`, plus\n   commonly-cited UK/FR examples). This is a genuinely new check-\n   family shape: the identifier proves or disproves itself, no second\n   field needed. Gates only `:actuation/post-settlement`.\n3. **A portability lesson, caught before any test ran.** A first\n   draft of the mod-97 computation used JVM-only `Character/isDigit`,\n   `Character/toUpperCase` and `int`-on-char arithmetic — this would\n   silently misbehave if the `.cljc` namespace were ever compiled for\n   ClojureScript. Rewritten to use portable `clojure.string`-based\n   digit lookups (single-character substrings + a string-keyed digit-\n   value map) before any test was written, keeping the file a real,\n   portable `.cljc`.\n4. **`sanctions-violations` — reuse of the established name, the 6th\n   literal grounding.** Verified via a literal `defn-` grep (not just\n   a docstring mention): `underwriting.governor`, `casualty.governor`\n   (the flagship original), `vcfund.governor`, `formation.governor`\n   and `realty.governor` all already have their own literal\n   `sanctions-violations` check. Sanctions screening is a genuinely\n   shared, industry-standard AML/OFAC concept across financial-\n   services verticals — unlike this fleet's domain-specific\n   \"safeguarding\"/\"risk\" concepts, reusing the identical name here is\n   the honest choice. Gates `:sanctions/screen` and `:actuation/\n   dispatch-interbank-message`.\n5. **No bespoke capability-lib dependency**, despite `blueprint.edn`\n   naming `:banking`/`:swift` as required technologies — following\n   every sibling actor's posture of implementing the specific ground-\n   truth check a governor needs directly (the real IBAN checksum)\n   rather than adding an external dependency for a scaffold this\n   narrow in scope.\n6. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard booleans.** `:settlement-\n   posted?`/`:interbank-message-dispatched?` on the `account` record.\n7. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/banking/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor is\n   safely named `account` directly.\n8. **Phase 0→3 rollout** — Phase 3 `:auto` set is `{:account/intake}`\n   only; both actuations are permanently excluded from every phase's\n   `:auto` set.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** — `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **`blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes** — corrected the stale\n    `:itonami.blueprint/id` and added the missing `:robotics` entry to\n    `:required-technologies`.\n11. **A pre-existing test-fixture repoint.** Promoting `6419` broke a\n    pre-existing `industry_test.clj` fixture that had hardcoded ISIC\n    `\"6419\"` as its generic \"some `:blueprint` entry\" example — caught\n    by re-running the full industry test suite before committing, and\n    repointed to `\"9411\"` (still `:blueprint`, confirmed with a real\n    repo) rather than deleting or weakening the assertions.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Fifty-third actor in this fleet (52 implemented before this build).\n- Establishes the first checksum/format-validity check family in this\n  fleet, backed by a real, standards-conformant algorithm.\n- Confirms the `sanctions-violations` concept generalizes cleanly to\n  a sixth grounding, the first in a deposit-taking/core-banking\n  context specifically.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity proven by contract test.\n- Two pre-existing `blueprint.edn` inconsistencies and one pre-\n  existing test-fixture assumption fixed as in-scope minor\n  consistency work.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 52 → 53, `:blueprint` 32 → 31,\n  `:spec` 546 unchanged, total 643.\n- Test status: 38 tests / 176 assertions (child repo), plus a\n  repointed 7 tests / 101 assertions (kotoba-lang/industry), all\n  green.\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| Add `kotoba-lang/banking`/`kotoba-lang/swift` as real `deps.edn` dependencies | Every sibling implements domain-specific ground-truth checks directly rather than depending on an external capability library; this would be a scope expansion beyond a `:blueprint`→`:implemented` promotion and introduce version-compatibility risk none of this fleet's other 52 actors carry |\n| Name the sanctions check something domain-specific | Sanctions screening is genuinely the same AML/OFAC concept across every financial-services vertical in this fleet (confirmed by reading, not just grepping, five siblings' own literal definitions) — reusing the exact name is the honest choice |\n| Implement the IBAN checksum with JVM `Character`/`int` interop (first draft) | Breaks ClojureScript portability, violating the `.cljc` discipline every sibling namespace follows — rewritten before any test was written |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6419/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6419/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6419/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"6419\"`)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 53, :blueprint 31, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/sanctions-screen-design-6419 "sanctions-violations REUSES the exact concept/name underwriting.governor/casualty.governor/vcfund.governor/formation.governor/realty.governor already established (verified via a literal defn- grep, not just a docstring mention) -- the SIXTH literal grounding of that exact name, and the THIRTY-SEVENTH distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall; unlike this fleet's domain-specific 'safeguarding'/'urgent-risk'/'dropout-risk' concepts (each needing its own name because they are NOT the same real-world concern), sanctions screening is a genuinely SHARED AML/OFAC compliance concept across financial-services verticals, so reusing the identical name here is the honest choice, not a naming-collision risk"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/blueprint-field-fixes-6419 "this promotion also corrected a stale pre-rename :itonami.blueprint/id field (\"cloud-itonami-6419\" -> \"cloud-itonami-isic-6419\") and added the previously-missing :robotics entry to :required-technologies (blueprint.edn already had :itonami.blueprint/robotics true set separately, but the required-technologies vector itself was missing :robotics, unlike the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"6419\" which already lists it) -- the same class of fix card/6619's, water/3600's, telecom/6190's, aerospace/3030's, fab/2610's, energy/3512's, care/8810's, navigator/8691's and learning/8569's own ADRs document"), (:adr/dual-actuation-6419 "two actuation events (:actuation/post-settlement, :actuation/dispatch-interbank-message) on the SAME account entity, matching 6512's/6622's/6520's/6530's/6820's/6920's/6611's/8530's/9200's/9521's/8730's/9102's/9103's/8890's/8610's/8510's/9412's/8720's/8521's/6619's/3600's/6190's/3030's/3830's/9420's/9491's/2610's/3512's/8810's/8691's/8569's dual-actuation shape, each with its own history/sequence/dedicated double-actuation boolean guard -- BOTH POSITIVE, matching this fleet's majority shape (3600/6190 remain the only negative-actuation exceptions)"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR, not an addendum to any prior financial-services sibling's ADR, because ISIC 6419 (community monetary intermediation / deposit-taking) has a genuinely distinct core-banking/clearing concern from brokerage/credit/accounting/marketadmin/card, warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention"), (:adr/test-fixture-repoint-6419 "promoting 6419 broke a PRE-EXISTING industry_test.clj fixture (maturity-tier / maturity-roadmap-reports-next-step / execution-plan-reports-ui-export-readiness) that had hardcoded ISIC \"6419\" as its generic 'some :blueprint entry' example -- caught by re-running the full industry test suite before committing (not assumed clean), and repointed to \"9411\" (Activities of business and employers membership organizations, confirmed still :blueprint with a real repo) rather than deleting or weakening the assertions"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/lesson-applied-proactively-6419 "tested via :sanctions/screen directly from the start (not via an actuation op against an unscreened account), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's and learning's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a twenty-seventh consecutive vertical"), (:adr/distinctive-check-6419 "iban-checksum-invalid? is the FIRST instance of this fleet's checksum/format-validity check family -- a REAL ISO 7064 MOD 97-10 IBAN validation (rearrange + letter-substitute + mod 97), not a fabricated placeholder, tested against well-known published IBAN examples (Deutsche Bundesbank's own DE89370400440532013000, plus commonly-cited UK/FR examples), a genuinely new check-family SHAPE (recomputes a checksum from the identifier's own characters, rather than comparing two already-trusted fields against each other or a threshold)"), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-6419"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-6419 (community monetary intermediation) deepened to :implemented -- thirty-ninth vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))